# Home Repo

Shared steering for {{GIT_USER}}'s repos, following the
[Home Repo pattern](https://www.aihero.dev/the-home-repo-pattern): shared docs, the
daily-report tower, and pointers to every other repo live here. **Start agent sessions in
this repo**; reach other repos through the pointers below.

Seeded by the `home-repo-bootstrap` skill. This file is yours now — edit it freely; the skill
never overwrites it unless you pass `-Force`.

## How to work from here

- Sessions start in this repo. To work on another repo, use its pointer: if the path exists,
  work there; if it does not, clone from the remote first.
- Give each feature its own worktree inside that repo's clone, so several agents can work one
  repo at once.
- Read a repo's own AGENTS.md first when it has one (hinted below).
- The paths below reflect one machine. A missing path is not an error — clone from the remote
  if missing. Committing these absolute paths is the documented exception to the
  "machine paths live only in the manifest" rule.

