## Skills

One rule: **a skill has exactly one source of truth** — an updater or a git repo — and it is
never copied to a second location.

- **Shared upstream skills** — git source `arisng/github-copilot-fc` (root `skills/`),
  installed and refreshed with `npx skills update -g` into `~/.agents/skills/` (tracked by
  `~/.agents/.skill-lock.json`). Do not copy them into any repo.
- **Plugin skills** — refreshed with `copilot plugin update --all`
  (`~/.copilot/installed-plugins/`).
- **Repo-level skills** — live only in their own repo and load only in sessions started there.
- **Canonical user-level store** — `~/.agents/skills/`. The personal dirs
  `~/.claude/skills/`, `~/.copilot/skills/` and `~/.codex/skills/` are junctions to it.

## Where things live

- `docs/` — shared coding standards (`docs/coding-standards.md`) and the standing glossary
  (`docs/glossary.md`).
- `reports/daily/` — the daily-report tower output; the per-machine manifest
  (`daily-report.manifest.json`) and exported transcripts stay gitignored.
- `scripts/local-ci.ps1` with `.githooks/pre-commit` — the whole CI: it validates staged
  reports and the pointers in this file; there is no cloud pipeline.
